---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = 'September 7, 2026';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Greg Weinger"
  description="How gweinger.com collects, uses, and protects your information."
>
  <div class="container legal">

    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">This policy explains what information gweinger.com collects, why, and what you can do about it.</p>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>
      gweinger.com is a personal website operated by Greg Weinger, publisher of
      <em>The Introverted Leader</em> podcast. You can reach me at
      <a href="mailto:greg@gweinger.com">greg@gweinger.com</a> or through the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What I collect</h2>

    <h3>When you visit a page</h3>
    <p>
      This site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare processes standard web request
      data — your IP address, browser type, and the pages you request — to deliver the site
      and protect it from abuse.
    </p>
    <p>
      I use Google Analytics 4 to understand which episodes and topics people find useful.
      It sets cookies and records the pages you view, an approximate location derived from
      your IP address, and basic device and browser information. I see this only as
      aggregate reporting — never as a way to identify you personally.
    </p>

    <h3>When you contact me</h3>
    <p>
      The contact form collects your name, email address, and message. That information is
      sent directly to my personal inbox so I can reply. It is not stored in a database on
      this site and it is not added to any mailing list.
    </p>

    <h3>When you sign up for something</h3>
    <p>
      Signup happens on my own sites, not on someone else's platform page. The masterclass
      and Leadership Labs forms on this site collect your email address (and, where the form
      asks, your first name or feedback) and submit it to <strong>Kit</strong>, the email
      service I use to run those lists and send you what you asked for.
    </p>
    <p>
      The newsletter lives at powerfulintrovertpodcast.com, also my own domain. It is
      published using <strong>Substack</strong>, so Substack stores and processes subscriber
      details for that list.
    </p>
    <p>
      Either way, your email address is used to send you the material you signed up for and
      related updates about the show. Every email includes an unsubscribe link, and I don't
      pass your address to anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2>Third parties that receive data</h2>
    <p>
      Some parts of this site load content from other companies. When they do, those
      companies receive your IP address and may set their own cookies, under their own
      privacy policies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics &amp; Google Fonts</strong> — analytics and the site's typeface (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>YouTube</strong> — embedded episode videos (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Simplecast</strong> — the embedded audio player (<a href="https://simplecast.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Kit</strong> — email service behind the masterclass and Labs signup forms (<a href="https://kit.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Substack</strong> — the platform publishing the newsletter at powerfulintrovertpodcast.com (<a href="https://substack.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>)</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting and email delivery (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What I don't do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>I don't sell your personal information.</li>
      <li>I don't share your contact form message with anyone else.</li>
      <li>I don't run advertising networks or retargeting pixels on this site.</li>
      <li>I don't attempt to identify individual visitors from analytics data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and how to opt out</h2>
    <p>
      The cookies on this site come from Google Analytics and from embedded players. You can
      block or delete cookies in your browser settings, and Google offers a
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">browser add-on to opt out of Analytics</a>
      entirely. The site works fine either way.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to request a copy of the personal
      information I hold about you, ask me to correct it, or ask me to delete it. For
      anything I hold directly — that is, an email you sent me — write to
      <a href="mailto:greg@gweinger.com">greg@gweinger.com</a> and I'll take care of it.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the email lists, you can manage or delete your subscription using the unsubscribe
      link in any email you receive, or by contacting me and I'll do it for you.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is intended for working professionals and is not directed at children under
      13. I don't knowingly collect information from them.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      Some links on this site — usually to books mentioned on the podcast — are affiliate
      links, meaning I may earn a small commission if you buy through them at no extra cost
      to you. Those merchants apply their own privacy policies once you leave this site.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes in a way that matters, I'll update the date at the top of this
      page. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:greg@gweinger.com">greg@gweinger.com</a> or use the
      <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
    </p>

  </div>

  <style>
    .legal { max-width: 46rem; }
    .legal h2 { margin-top: var(--space-8); }
    .legal h3 { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
    .legal p, .legal li { line-height: 1.7; }
    .legal ul { margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); padding-left: var(--space-6); }
    .legal li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
    .legal-updated {
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    }
  </style>
</Base>
